messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Global fossil carbon dioxide emissions peak.",
      "detail": "Coal use plateaus and then falls as solar, wind, batteries, and electric vehicles continue rapid growth; emissions begin an uneven decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "Global average temperature reaches 1.5 degrees Celsius above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "The Paris aspirational threshold is breached as a multi-year average. Heatwaves and extreme rainfall become more severe but not civilization-ending."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "First AI-designed broad-spectrum antibiotic is approved.",
      "detail": "Generative molecular design reaches clinical practice, shortening drug discovery times and opening a wave of AI-designed medicines."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "Renewables supply more than 60 percent of global electricity.",
      "detail": "Solar and wind are the cheapest power sources in most regions; gas peaker plants remain for reliability but their use declines."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "Managed retreat begins in exposed coastal cities.",
      "detail": "Several governments start buying out and relocating neighborhoods in Miami, Jakarta, Lagos, and the Nile Delta because of sea-level rise and storm surges."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Climate-driven migration crisis peaks in tropical regions.",
      "detail": "Repeated heatwaves, crop failures, and water stress force tens of millions to move within and across borders. It fuels conflict but does not lead to a global war."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence is demonstrated.",
      "detail": "A system can reason across domains at roughly human level, though it is costly and error-prone. It accelerates research and automation but remains under human oversight."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Global unemployment from AI automation reaches a disruptive peak.",
      "detail": "Large parts of routine cognitive work are automated. Many countries adopt basic income, retraining, and reduced workweeks, but social disruption is severe."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "First commercial fusion plant supplies grid power.",
      "detail": "Net-energy fusion moves from experiment to early commercial deployment. It does not replace renewables but provides clean baseload power."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Global human population peaks near 9.5 billion.",
      "detail": "Falling fertility outweighs rising longevity. Population then begins a slow, long-term decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global carbon dioxide emissions become net-negative.",
      "detail": "Carbon removal via direct air capture, bioenergy with carbon capture, and enhanced weathering exceeds residual emissions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Sea-level rise reaches 0.6 meters above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Coastal megacities have poured trillions into barriers, pumps, and elevated infrastructure; many smaller communities are abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Ice-free Arctic summers become regular.",
      "detail": "The Arctic Ocean is essentially ice-free each September. Shipping routes expand but Arctic ecosystems are severely disrupted."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Global average temperature stabilizes near 2.1 degrees Celsius above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "After sustained net-negative emissions, temperatures stop rising. Extreme weather remains worse than present but slowly stabilizes."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Ectogenesis becomes a minority but accepted form of human reproduction.",
      "detail": "Synthetic wombs become safe and commercially available. They reduce maternal mortality and alter debates about reproduction, gender, and work."
    },
    {
      "year": 2110,
      "event": "A limited nuclear exchange occurs between regional powers.",
      "detail": "Two small nuclear-armed states use a handful of weapons in a border war. Millions die, but escalation to a global strategic exchange is avoided."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Permanent lunar settlement becomes self-sustaining in life support.",
      "detail": "The Moon base produces its own water, food, and oxygen from polar ice and regolith. Population is several hundred."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "Mars settlement reaches 100,000 people.",
      "detail": "Early colonies are sustained by Earth imports but develop local water, food, and manufacturing capacity. Birth on Mars begins."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Asteroid mining supplies much of Earth's rare metals.",
      "detail": "Platinum-group metals and other minerals from near-Earth asteroids reduce terrestrial mining damage and fund space infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Human lifespan commonly exceeds 120 years.",
      "detail": "Genetic, cellular, and organ-replacement therapies become widely available. Aging is slowed but not eliminated."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Earth's human population stabilizes around 5 billion.",
      "detail": "Long-term low fertility and voluntary population decline lead to a smaller, older, wealthier, but less dynamic global population."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Large orbital habitats house millions of people.",
      "detail": "Rotating habitats in Earth orbit and cislunar space form the first generation of permanent off-world homes. They are economically linked to Earth and the Moon."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Human settlement on Mars reaches one million people.",
      "detail": "Mars becomes a self-governing and mostly self-sufficient society. Its residents begin to adapt culturally and physically to lower gravity."
    },
    {
      "year": 3400,
      "event": "Interstellar probe arrives at Proxima Centauri.",
      "detail": "A small robotic craft launched centuries earlier sends back close images of the nearest exoplanet. It finds no technosignature but confirms a rocky world."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "First generation ship departs for a nearby star.",
      "detail": "A large, slow vessel carrying several thousand people begins a multi-century journey. Its destination is a planet orbiting a nearby M-dwarf."
    },
    {
      "year": 4200,
      "event": "Earth's ice sheets reach a new equilibrium.",
      "detail": "After centuries of slow melt and regrowth at higher latitudes, the Greenland and West Antarctic ice sheets stabilize at smaller volumes. Sea level is about four meters above 2000."
    },
    {
      "year": 4600,
      "event": "Biological and cybernetic human variants become recognized.",
      "detail": "Off-world populations have adapted through gene editing and implants for radiation resistance, low gravity, and different atmospheres. Earth humans are one branch among several."
    },
    {
      "year": 5200,
      "event": "A solar-system-scale civilization exists.",
      "detail": "Earth, Mars, the Moon, and orbital habitats contain billions of humans and human variants. They are loosely connected by trade and data but politically fragmented."
    },
    {
      "year": 5800,
      "event": "Earth biodiversity is largely restored.",
      "detail": "De-extinction, rewilding, and carbon removal have restored many ecosystems. Large mammals and engineered species fill lost ecological niches."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "First interstellar colony beyond the Sun becomes self-sustaining.",
      "detail": "A settlement around another star reaches several thousand people and no longer depends on Earth for survival."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "A rare extreme solar storm severely damages Earth's orbital infrastructure.",
      "detail": "The flare destroys many satellites and power grids. Civilization absorbs the shock within decades, but dependence on space is temporarily reduced."
    },
    {
      "year": 8200,
      "event": "Earth's political organization consolidates into regional unions.",
      "detail": "After repeated ecological and economic crises, a small number of continental-scale unions manage climate, biosphere, and migration. No single world state exists."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human descendants on Mars and orbital habitats become reproductively isolated.",
      "detail": "Differences in gravity, genetics, and culture make natural interbreeding with Earth populations difficult. They are considered distinct human species or subspecies."
    },
    {
      "year": 9600,
      "event": "Interstellar communication network links several colonies.",
      "detail": "Light-speed links connect small human populations around several nearby stars. Each solar system is largely self-governing."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity is a multi-system, multi-species civilization.",
      "detail": "Total population across the solar system and a few nearby stars is roughly 10 billion. Earth remains historically central but no longer dominant. No extinction event has occurred."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity survives the next several centuries of climate disruption, AI-driven transformation, and demographic decline, then expands into the solar system and nearby stars. It becomes a multi-planetary, genetically and culturally diverse civilization without a single unified state. The highest-risk period is the next few centuries, but in this forecast no extinction event occurs."
}
